 @realfeils4655  Well for starters I didn't claim 100%+ extra performance. I also don't have any other stuff running in the background since it was tested on a new build. It just happens that the FPS saw a steep increase for this specific game. In Stellar Blade it went from ~70-80 to ~120ish.

The version of RX 9060 XT I am currently using is the Yeston OC Gaming Ace if that matters. Went from stock low 60's fps to 100 as soon as I flicked it into OC mode. The only settings I changed in Andrenalin were -40 undervolt and  +10% wattage. No framegen no FSR, just pure native ultra settings (of course with RT/PT off as well).

If I were to enable FSR Quality in Cyberpunk, it shoots up to ~170-180fps. Was not expecting much from the GPU when I first got it due to reviews of it being "1440p entry", but after owning it and playing with it, I can vouch that it's beyond just an entry card.

 @LuksOngs  I haven't had to change any ingame settings in Andrenalin so it's most likely not it. The only thing I did to see this kind of a performance increase was flipping the BIOs switch on the card.

Before flipping it I'm seeing low 60s in Cyberpunk, after enabling it my fps jumped up to steady high 100s. In between and after changing the card's BIOs mode, I have not changed any settings on the PC itself, it was a straight boot up and launch into game.

Trust me when I say that most of these benchmarks videos are not showing the card at it's full potential. These common 60 fps are on a bone stock 9060 XT and I was also not a believer/expecting much from it since I was also only getting information from these before purchasing and owning the card myself. If any of you have an OC switch on the card, just flip it on and enjoy.
